1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,560
Suzuki.

2
00:00:01,560 --> 00:00:03,690
Do you still read that BL crap?

3
00:00:03,690 --> 00:00:05,390
Quit harassing

4
00:00:05,390 --> 00:00:08,430
our Suzuki.

5
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:09,730
I'm a fellow BL lover, too.

6
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:11,730
We've read a bit, as well.

7
00:00:11,730 --> 00:00:16,150
I feel so welcomed here.

8
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:18,580
I'm having so much fun right now.

9
00:00:20,690 --> 00:00:23,370
Cute!

10
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:27,760
<i>I've become friends with the popular guys.</i>

11
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:29,350
- Looks good.
- Suzuki.

12
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:31,120
- Fried chicken?
- Open wide.

13
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:33,750
And fried rice, the usual.

14
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:35,100
Homemade, I assume?

15
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:36,270
That's my girlfriend for you!

16
00:00:36,270 --> 00:00:38,780
Show off.

17
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:40,540
Now let's dig in.

18
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:45,030
So, that set-up was to help Suzuki write.

19
00:00:45,030 --> 00:00:46,460
Makes sense.

20
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:48,510
And here I thought Serizawa was being weird.

21
00:00:48,510 --> 00:00:50,800
He still is.

22
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,180
Touche.

23
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:56,730
<i>Now, I can openly talk about BL with them.</i>

24
00:00:56,730 --> 00:00:59,180
Are you actually able to write like that?

25
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:03,080
Yeah. Bit by bit.

26
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:05,870
I see.

27
00:01:05,870 --> 00:01:08,080
Let me read what you have so far.

28
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:09,850
You're not a novel guy, though.

29
00:01:09,850 --> 00:01:12,820
I'd read Suzuki's work.

30
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:19,300
You know who Suzuki reminds me of
when I feed him?

31
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:21,830
Usami.

32
00:01:21,830 --> 00:01:23,820
Usami...

33
00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:24,850
Our teacher?

34
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:26,630
<i>All right, let's start with warm-ups.</i>

35
00:01:26,630 --> 00:01:28,070
<i>Find a partner and get stretching.</i>

36
00:01:28,070 --> 00:01:32,120
He's talking about a rabbit
he met in our first year,

37
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:34,470
during that field trip we took to a farm.

38
00:01:34,470 --> 00:01:36,490
- A rabbit.
- Yeah.

39
00:01:36,490 --> 00:01:41,270
Serizawa kept feeding the poor thing.

40
00:01:41,270 --> 00:01:43,570
Eventually, it became too bloated to move.

41
00:01:43,570 --> 00:01:46,730
I felt so bad for it

42
00:01:46,730 --> 00:01:48,110
He totally overfed that rabbit.

43
00:01:48,110 --> 00:01:51,310
But it was just so cute.

44
00:01:51,310 --> 00:01:53,980
I wish I could've brought it home with me.

45
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:55,850
Careful, Suzuki.

46
00:01:55,850 --> 00:01:58,850
This guy can get seriously possessive.

47
00:01:58,850 --> 00:01:59,890
What?

48
00:01:59,890 --> 00:02:01,920
I do not.

49
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:04,410
Besides, I'm a noble top.

50
00:02:04,410 --> 00:02:06,310
Isn't that right, Suzuki?

51
00:02:06,310 --> 00:02:08,040
"Noble"?

52
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:09,470
More like, selfish.

53
00:02:09,470 --> 00:02:11,960
- Agreed.
- Right?

54
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:14,860
Noble, my ass.

55
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:16,660
<i>But...</i>

56
00:02:31,710 --> 00:02:35,320
Sorry. You had ketchup on your cheek.

57
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:38,900
It's fine. Thanks.

58
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:42,870
<i>Sometimes, I get a bit confused.</i>

59
00:02:47,650 --> 00:02:50,710
Suzuki, you're like a twig.

60
00:02:50,710 --> 00:02:52,750
Do you eat enough?

61
00:02:54,330 --> 00:02:56,580
Don't grope the guy.

62
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:03,140
Eat well, and grow up strong, okay?

63
00:03:03,990 --> 00:03:06,200
What are you, his mom?

64
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:09,600
<i>Is this something friends do?</i>

65
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:11,190
Mom?

66
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:13,580
- He's his Seri-Mom.
- Yeah.

67
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:15,430
That's a mom for you.

68
00:03:59,310 --> 00:04:00,130
[Episode 4]

69
00:04:00,130 --> 00:04:03,440
Really? Aw man...

70
00:04:04,110 --> 00:04:06,530
All right, who's out today?

71
00:04:06,530 --> 00:04:08,190
Serizawa?

72
00:04:08,190 --> 00:04:10,360
- That's unusual.
- What happened?

73
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:12,410
- He caught a cold.
- Is he okay?

74
00:04:12,410 --> 00:04:15,630
Yeah. He got the medicine he needs.

75
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:17,280
I'm sure he'll be fine.

76
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:19,340
I mean, look at the way he's spamming us.

77
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:20,520
[The Gang]

78
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:22,450
<i>Hello?</i>

79
00:04:22,450 --> 00:04:24,620
<i>Dog.</i>

80
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:27,920
<i>Gouche.</i>

81
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:30,600
Are you sure he's okay?

82
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:35,100
He's just playing a word game
against himself.

83
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:36,640
It's his usual routine.

84
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:38,420
He's totally bored.

85
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:39,640
And he lost?

86
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:41,700
Hilarious!

87
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:45,640
The classroom's super quiet
without him around though.

88
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:48,040
[Pudding]

89
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:56,850
Serizawa's on class duty today?

90
00:04:56,850 --> 00:04:59,190
Too bad, I had a favor to ask.

91
00:04:59,190 --> 00:05:01,180
I'll fill in for him.

92
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:06,040
I knew if anyone would step up, you would.

93
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,440
Thanks, Takeuchi.

94
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:08,800
Of course.

95
00:05:27,270 --> 00:05:29,560
Takeuchi.

96
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,010
Suzuki?

97
00:05:31,010 --> 00:05:32,070
I'll help.

98
00:05:32,070 --> 00:05:34,430
Really? Then could you
take the stuff on top?

99
00:05:34,430 --> 00:05:36,340
- Sure.
- Thanks.

100
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:40,090
Did you get a response from Serizawa?

101
00:05:40,090 --> 00:05:41,340
I told you, not yet.

102
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:43,690
How many times will you ask?

103
00:05:48,550 --> 00:05:52,380
[Serizawa, are you okay?]
[Is there anything you need?]

104
00:05:57,590 --> 00:05:59,490
Something up?

105
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:03,680
Well...

106
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:06,740
I was just wondering if Serizawa was okay.

107
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:12,020
We haven't heard from him since this morning.

108
00:06:16,140 --> 00:06:19,130
Oh no, what if he fainted?

109
00:06:23,290 --> 00:06:25,390
Suzuki.

110
00:06:27,170 --> 00:06:31,620
I don't know if I'm allowed to ask, but...

111
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:36,630
Do you...

112
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:41,390
Like Serizawa?

113
00:06:41,390 --> 00:06:43,000
Huh?

114
00:06:44,790 --> 00:06:48,140
Sorry, if you're not comfortable answering...

115
00:06:48,140 --> 00:06:51,450
No, I mean. I do think Serizawa's cool.

116
00:06:51,450 --> 00:06:53,760
But he's only my model top.

117
00:06:54,570 --> 00:06:56,310
I see.

118
00:06:56,310 --> 00:07:02,020
Yeah. Besides, I've never really...

119
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:08,220
fallen in love before.

120
00:07:09,230 --> 00:07:10,740
Not even once?

121
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:13,420
You know I'm a nervous wreck.

122
00:07:13,420 --> 00:07:16,270
And I always get really anxious.

123
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:20,700
So, romance is a high hurdle for me.

124
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:23,330
I don't really get it, either.

125
00:07:23,330 --> 00:07:27,690
You don't get it, huh.

126
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:32,910
Then let me ask you this.

127
00:07:32,910 --> 00:07:37,490
You've never felt your heart beat faster

128
00:07:37,490 --> 00:07:39,510
when you're around Serizawa?

129
00:07:40,850 --> 00:07:42,860
What?

130
00:07:47,910 --> 00:07:50,570
'Sup.

131
00:07:50,570 --> 00:07:52,220
Sir.

132
00:07:53,030 --> 00:07:55,440
I've finished up today's logs.

133
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,640
Thanks.

134
00:07:56,640 --> 00:08:00,900
[Class Logs]

135
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:02,670
Wow, Takeuchi.

136
00:08:02,670 --> 00:08:04,900
You're as meticulous as ever.

137
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:07,010
Thank you.

138
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:11,130
Suzuki, thanks for helping him out.

139
00:08:12,850 --> 00:08:14,630
Huh?

140
00:08:14,630 --> 00:08:17,320
Suzuki? Hello?

141
00:08:20,790 --> 00:08:22,940
He's frozen up.

142
00:08:27,930 --> 00:08:30,200
My heart beating faster...

143
00:08:35,390 --> 00:08:39,310
<i>Does that count?</i>

144
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:41,480
<i>Pinky promise.</i>

145
00:08:42,630 --> 00:08:46,650
<i>What about that?</i>

146
00:08:46,650 --> 00:08:48,210
<i>Here, let me see.</i>

147
00:08:48,830 --> 00:08:50,290
<i>Huh?</i>

148
00:08:50,290 --> 00:08:52,400
<i>Wait a second.</i>

149
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:55,030
<i>Sorry!</i>

150
00:08:55,850 --> 00:08:58,060
<i>He makes my heart go crazy.</i>

151
00:08:58,060 --> 00:09:00,260
No, no, no.

152
00:09:01,210 --> 00:09:03,760
<i>I mean, sure, my heart rate increases.</i>

153
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:07,220
<i>But that's because Serizawa is my ideal top.</i>

154
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:09,930
<i>That's all.</i>

155
00:09:19,450 --> 00:09:21,660
I miss him.

156
00:09:22,650 --> 00:09:25,160
No, I don't!

157
00:09:31,470 --> 00:09:32,580
[Notification]

158
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:34,850
<i>Suzuki, I want to see you.</i>

159
00:09:44,540 --> 00:09:48,130
<i>I actually came to see him.</i>

160
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:51,690
[Serizawa]

161
00:09:51,690 --> 00:09:57,480
<i>But he probably wasn't serious.</i>

162
00:10:11,050 --> 00:10:13,430
<i>"Serizawa, are you awake?"</i>

163
00:10:13,430 --> 00:10:17,550
<i>"I brought your schoolwork
and some pudding."</i>

164
00:10:17,550 --> 00:10:19,600
<i>"I'll leave them at the front gate."</i>

165
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:21,460
<i>"Take care."</i>

166
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,070
Suzuki.

167
00:10:29,510 --> 00:10:31,390
Serizawa?

168
00:10:33,830 --> 00:10:37,690
You really came.

169
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:49,730
Uh, I...

170
00:10:49,730 --> 00:10:51,100
You can come in.

171
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:53,490
No one else is home.

172
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:58,600
Thanks for having me.

173
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,980
This is my room.

174
00:11:09,980 --> 00:11:12,940
<i>Serizawa's room...</i>

175
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:14,900
And this...

176
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:17,580
is my collection.

177
00:11:20,830 --> 00:11:23,360
You have all my favorites!

178
00:11:26,090 --> 00:11:28,910
<i>He's got an impressive collection.</i>

179
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,280
Come join me.

180
00:11:40,910 --> 00:11:42,510
Sure.

181
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:50,780
<i>I'm on Serizawa's bed.</i>

182
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:54,740
<i>Serizawa's in his roomwear.</i>

183
00:11:55,980 --> 00:11:59,050
<i>Longer sleeves... Un-styled hair...</i>

184
00:11:59,050 --> 00:12:02,510
<i>Wow... he looks so cool...</i>

185
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:06,800
<i>No, what am I thinking?</i>

186
00:12:08,830 --> 00:12:11,770
Were you able to find my place easily?

187
00:12:12,970 --> 00:12:16,510
Yeah. Takeuchi guided me here.

188
00:12:16,510 --> 00:12:18,170
Takeuchi?

189
00:12:18,170 --> 00:12:20,080
Yeah.

190
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:25,530
I didn't know you two
were friends from middle school.

191
00:12:25,530 --> 00:12:28,850
He told me you both live near by.

192
00:12:28,850 --> 00:12:30,230
Yeah.

193
00:12:30,230 --> 00:12:34,310
Did you walk here with Serizawa?

194
00:12:34,310 --> 00:12:38,730
Yeah. I invited him to join us,

195
00:12:38,730 --> 00:12:41,380
but he said he couldn't visit today.

196
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:42,920
I see.

197
00:12:43,790 --> 00:12:47,240
Who did you eat lunch with today?

198
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:51,460
I ate with the others like we usually do.

199
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:54,780
Did you talk to any of the girls today?

200
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:57,680
No, not really.

201
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:59,280
Why?

202
00:13:00,050 --> 00:13:01,690
No reason.

203
00:13:02,310 --> 00:13:06,000
I was just a bit worried.

204
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,580
Worried?

205
00:13:07,580 --> 00:13:08,980
Yeah.

206
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:16,950
Look.

207
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:21,950
I'm glad you're getting along
with the class now.

208
00:13:21,950 --> 00:13:25,200
But make sure I'm always
your number one, okay?

209
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:28,510
- What?
- Your answer?

210
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:34,030
Well?

211
00:13:34,030 --> 00:13:35,460
Uh...

212
00:13:36,710 --> 00:13:39,840
Okay.

213
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:44,010
I'm serious.

214
00:13:44,810 --> 00:13:49,220
<i>What is this?</i>

215
00:14:04,470 --> 00:14:06,310
Suzuki.

216
00:14:07,070 --> 00:14:10,490
Your ears are turning red.

217
00:14:12,830 --> 00:14:17,670
That's because I'm nervous.

218
00:14:18,490 --> 00:14:20,540
Nervous?

219
00:14:20,540 --> 00:14:22,690
You're nervous?

220
00:14:24,010 --> 00:14:26,930
Well, I mean...

221
00:14:26,930 --> 00:14:31,110
Does that mean I make your heart beat faster?

222
00:14:33,790 --> 00:14:36,450
I think, I'm...

223
00:14:36,450 --> 00:14:38,200
Serizawa?

224
00:14:43,730 --> 00:14:45,240
Huh?

225
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:49,430
Serizawa? Are you okay?

226
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:51,270
- Serizawa?
- I...

227
00:14:51,270 --> 00:14:53,120
I feel hot...

228
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:57,200
What should I do?

229
00:15:07,810 --> 00:15:09,490
You're awake.

230
00:15:10,990 --> 00:15:14,410
Did I fall asleep?

231
00:15:14,410 --> 00:15:16,540
Yeah. How do you feel?

232
00:15:17,730 --> 00:15:20,100
First, drink some water.

233
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:21,870
Thanks.

234
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:39,810
I feel way better now.

235
00:15:39,810 --> 00:15:41,850
What a relief.

236
00:15:41,850 --> 00:15:45,120
I was afraid you fainted on me.

237
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:48,480
Are you drinking your medicine?

238
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:49,940
Yeah.

239
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:51,290
How's your appetite?

240
00:15:51,290 --> 00:15:54,770
I bought some pudding, if you're hungry.

241
00:15:54,770 --> 00:15:56,530
Did you want any?

242
00:15:59,430 --> 00:16:03,680
I'll eat, if you feed me.

243
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:05,460
You can feed yourself!

244
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:08,990
Aw, but I'm always feeding you.

245
00:16:08,990 --> 00:16:13,180
Besides, a weakened top
is good material, right?

246
00:16:13,990 --> 00:16:17,100
I can't deny that.

247
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:22,300
Fine.

248
00:16:37,450 --> 00:16:38,900
Here.

249
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:45,640
How's that?

250
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:51,100
Delicious.

251
00:16:51,100 --> 00:16:53,730
It hits the spot.

252
00:16:57,180 --> 00:16:58,510
What's up?

253
00:16:58,510 --> 00:17:00,030
Nothing, it's just...

254
00:17:00,970 --> 00:17:05,530
You really are like the sun, Serizawa.

255
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,650
The sun?

256
00:17:07,650 --> 00:17:09,250
Yeah.

257
00:17:09,250 --> 00:17:10,930
You know...

258
00:17:10,930 --> 00:17:13,040
<i>I first got to know you</i>
[Year 2, Class 1]

259
00:17:13,040 --> 00:17:17,040
<i>when we were placed into the same class,
in our sophomore year.</i>

260
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:18,250
Serizawa!

261
00:17:18,250 --> 00:17:19,680
We're all together!

262
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:23,040
Yay!

263
00:17:23,040 --> 00:17:24,590
I am here!

264
00:17:24,590 --> 00:17:26,240
Yes, you are.

265
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:27,640
Thanks, Mr. Obvious.

266
00:17:27,640 --> 00:17:29,810
Dude, come on!

267
00:17:29,810 --> 00:17:34,360
<i>At the time, I knew of you
because you had a reputation.</i>

268
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:38,350
<i>But I didn't know you well.</i>

269
00:17:40,170 --> 00:17:41,780
<i>Until, one day...</i>

270
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:51,700
Suzuki, you dropped this.

271
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:53,160
Here.

272
00:17:54,410 --> 00:17:56,840
Thanks.

273
00:17:56,840 --> 00:18:01,650
<i>After spending time in class together...</i>

274
00:18:04,230 --> 00:18:07,470
Suzuki. We're going out as a class after this.

275
00:18:07,470 --> 00:18:09,780
Wanna join?

276
00:18:12,150 --> 00:18:16,590
Sorry. I'm not good at social events.

277
00:18:16,590 --> 00:18:17,700
No worries.

278
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:20,070
Sorry to put you on the spot.

279
00:18:20,070 --> 00:18:22,680
<i>I realized you were kind to everyone,</i>

280
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:26,970
<i>without any prejudice in your heart.</i>

281
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:33,910
<i>Whenever you smiled,
it made others happy, too.</i>

282
00:18:37,820 --> 00:18:41,340
<i>Though school had become a drag for me,</i>

283
00:18:43,180 --> 00:18:47,590
<i>your sunny presence changed that.</i>

284
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:57,860
So, class today without you,

285
00:18:59,730 --> 00:19:01,810
felt especially lonely.

286
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:08,310
Aw, man.

287
00:19:08,310 --> 00:19:10,660
That makes me super happy to hear.

288
00:19:15,490 --> 00:19:17,560
Hold on a second.

289
00:19:17,560 --> 00:19:20,230
You think I'm like the sun?

290
00:19:24,770 --> 00:19:27,140
Right, your fever.

291
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:29,250
Has it gone down already?

292
00:19:36,630 --> 00:19:41,170
I can't tell with my cold hands.

293
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:44,250
Huh?

294
00:19:44,250 --> 00:19:47,230
Don't pull back, okay?

295
00:19:58,140 --> 00:20:01,900
Seems like your fever's gone down.

296
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,810
S-Sorry!

297
00:20:09,530 --> 00:20:11,240
It's fine.

298
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:13,650
Thanks for checking.

299
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:17,550
I'm fine now.

300
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:19,740
Right.

301
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:22,860
That's good.

302
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:27,840
Rest up, okay?

303
00:20:27,840 --> 00:20:31,250
I'll be heading out now.

304
00:20:35,850 --> 00:20:37,330
No.

305
00:20:37,330 --> 00:20:39,140
Don't go.

306
00:20:40,570 --> 00:20:46,690
But your folks... Won't they be back soon?

307
00:20:46,690 --> 00:20:50,530
Nope. I'm alone today.

308
00:20:50,530 --> 00:20:52,920
- Huh?
- Mom's working the night shift.

309
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:55,250
Dad's living apart for his job.

310
00:20:55,250 --> 00:20:59,080
And my sister's on vacation with her friends.

311
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:02,330
So...

312
00:21:02,330 --> 00:21:04,750
Stay, please?

313
00:21:08,790 --> 00:21:11,460
I'll be lonely.

314
00:21:11,460 --> 00:21:13,380
Let's sleep together.

315
00:21:17,380 --> 00:21:19,820
[Serizawa]

316
00:21:23,590 --> 00:21:27,380
<i>What exactly is going on here?</i>

317
00:21:27,380 --> 00:21:31,110
Serizawa, I really should be...

318
00:21:31,110 --> 00:21:35,530
Turn away from me.
I don't want you catching my cold.

319
00:21:39,870 --> 00:21:41,660
Hey!

320
00:21:46,990 --> 00:21:49,890
I sleep easier like this.

321
00:21:49,890 --> 00:21:52,780
You're being way too selfish...

322
00:21:54,230 --> 00:21:58,680
Is your heart beating faster?

323
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:01,020
N-No!

324
00:22:02,830 --> 00:22:04,810
Cute.

325
00:22:04,810 --> 00:22:07,340
Shut up!

326
00:22:09,310 --> 00:22:11,660
<i>What do I do?</i>

327
00:22:11,660 --> 00:22:14,690
<i>This is bad.</i>

328
00:22:16,650 --> 00:22:18,680
Sorry, I'm going home!

329
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:22,680
No. Don't go.

330
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:24,720
Stay here till morning.

331
00:22:27,080 --> 00:22:29,180
Until morning?

332
00:22:30,020 --> 00:22:34,830
<i>My heart's going to explode!</i>

333
00:22:44,160 --> 00:22:50,040
<i>Maybe...</i>

334
00:22:51,270 --> 00:22:53,630
<i>I really do...</i>

335
00:22:56,780 --> 00:22:58,800
<i>like Serizawa.</i>

336
00:23:09,930 --> 00:23:11,930
Suzuki.

337
00:23:11,930 --> 00:23:14,900
You like me, don't you?

